==Strategy==
Mr. Mer is the star of the show, with the health of a tank and a dangerous sniping range of ''732.5 units'' thanks to his [[Mini-Wave]]s, a threat only compounded by how fragile many of your [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitters]] are. To make matters worse, there's a second layer of snipers in the form of Loincloth Cats who, while normally aren't too threatening on their own, can easily hide behind the Metal forces and quickly stack into a wall of DPS that will pick off your attackers if they can even move forward. With heavy pushers like Super Metal Hippoes, Metal One Horns and a Sir Metal Seal for good measure, you'll need much more than just good luck to make it out on top.

The most feasible way to beat this stage involves using long-range attackers like [[:Category:Waver-class Cats|Wavers]], [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]] and [[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge Attackers]] to kill the Mr. Mer and allow your Critters to clean up the Metals. Hold back the Metals as much as you can with stallers like [[Talents|Talented]] [[Panties Cat (Special Cat)|Lollycat]] and [[Clockwork Cat (Rare Cat)|Puppetmaster]] and hope to send them off with lucky crits from units like [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]] and [[Volley Cat (Rare Cat)|Curry Cat]] so they hopefully don't push too far into your attackers. Once the Mer-Lion dies, the Metals shouldn't be too hard to handle and hopefully you can clean them out with your Critters much more easily, though the stack of Loincloths might still prove to be troublesome without some [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|snipers]], [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|rushers]] or a well-timed [[Ototo Corps#Thunderbolt|Thunderbolt]].

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitters]]: Because of the backliners, anything that's easily replaceable and can deliver crits quickly is very recommended. [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]] is a reliable staple as always, but [[Volley Cat (Rare Cat)|Curry Cat]] and [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]] are also excellent picks due to their extra range. [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Catyphoon]] can help greatly for the Doges and Metal One Horns especially at the stage start, though they won't fare too well against the Super Metal Hippoes and Metal Seals once they come in.
*[[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]]: With immunity to waves and extreme Long-Range damage to Traitless, Hitman can effectively delete the Mr. Mer and make the stage much easier to handle, so long as they aren't rushed down by the Metals and don't waltz into the Loincloths' range.
*[[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Mightycat]]: As a rusher with [[Wave Shield]] and weaken to Traitless, he can swoop in to buy your critters more time to land some good blows. His many knockbacks coupled with the sheer DPS of the enemies leaves his usefulness in blocking waves and hitting procs a little more dubious, so careful timing is recommended.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]]: With careful timing as well to avoid the Mini-Waves, Slime can abuse the Metals as stepping stones to burst tons of damage to Mr. Mer and especially the Loincloths, making it a very powerful ally for this stage. True Form is recommended to make its devastation much easier.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Panties Cat (Special Cat)|Lollycat]]: When the slow Metal Talent is maxed out, Lollycat becomes a surprisingly competent anti-Metal for this stage, even at just Lv.30 without any of their stat Talents. They have a quick recharge, decent chance to proc and Area Attack on top of their decent range allowing them to stay safe from the Loincloth Cats. Beware that Mr. Mer will absolutely destroy any stacks of them, so unless a ranged Wave Blocker is used or Mr. Mer is dead, they will not be of much use.
*[[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Jagando Jr.]]: Surges, knockback and strong vs. Traitless allow him to nullify Mr. Mer from harassing your critters while dealing strong damage to him as well.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Izanami of Dusk (Legend Rare Cat)|Izanami of Eventide]]: Her insane damage vs. Traitless and far-piercing attacks allow her to snipe and kill the Loincloth Cats even when they are standing behind the Metal enemies, preventing them from stacking up. She can also kill the Mr. Mer quickly and her Conjure acts as a secondary Breakerblast to push away the enemies, but beware that it may allow your Critical hitters to enter the Loincloth Cats' range.

